== Impact from stats ==

Mages are fairly simple to gear for as there is basically only one primary stat.

*'''Strength'''       - For Magicians this is mostly carry weight for loot. Mages are the least strength dependant class in the game. They don't melee past the very first few levels and they have a way easier time time carrying loot with their weightless and 100% weight reducing bags that they can summon.
*'''Stamina'''        - Gives a minor increase in maximum Hit Points. Magicians should very rarely get hit, so it's not as useful to them even in min/maxing.
*'''Dexterity'''      - Mainly involved in raising weapon skills and proccing weapon effects.
*'''Agility'''        - Adds to your ability to avoiding being struck with physical attacks and lowers the damage you take from physical attacks on average. If Erudite is your race choice know that agility less than 75 isn't just poor, it's penalized, consider putting 5 points in to remove the penalty.
*'''Wisdom'''         - Stat used to calculate how fast you learn general and craft skills if it is higher than your Intelligence.
*'''Intelligence'''   - Influences how much maximum mana you gain per level and the rate at which you learn spell skills. Used to calculate how fast you learn general and craft skills if higher than Wisdom. Your maximum mana dictates how many spells you can cast before you are forced to rest.
*'''Charisma'''       - Influences the price you pay to vendors for their goods, and the price they pay you for your goods. How well liked you are by the faction the merchant belongs to factors into this.
== Religion ==

Generally speaking being agnostic is a fairly safe bet in Everquest. Follower of [[Tunare]] can quest for [[Chord of Vines]].

